this is tony wilson reading mike  epstein's review of bug snacks  sometimes the name is the game bug  snacks the new game from octodad  developer young horses  is all about catching bugs made of  traditionally appetizing foods like  pizza  strawberries carrots and lollipops which  turn your body parts into food when you  eat them  they're bugs but they're made of snacks  bug  snacks bug snacks it's a wacky conceit  that when paired with the game's cute  and colorful art style puts a smile  on your face and pushes your imagination  to run wild  the surprisingly powerful desire to  discover more about these weird and  wonderful creatures fuels every aspect  of the experience  it's clever if somewhat temperamental  puzzles revolve around catching bug  snacks  the story sends you off to investigate  the mysteries of their home  snacktooth island and its colonists and  though that drive is purely superficial  the game you experience along the way  has a lot of substance  how do i even begin to explain what's  happening in bug snacks  you control an investigative journalist  who's reporting on the expedition of  explorer lizbert megafig to snacktooth  island  where she's discovered evidence of an  ancient civilization  and the delicious mysterious bug snacks  when you arrive  lisboard has gone missing and her colony  snacksberg has disbanded  your goal is to find the colonists  around the island and convince them to  get back together so you can get your  story and find out what happened to the  lost explorer  the world of bug snacks is colorful like  something out of a children's book  all of the humanoid characters are furry  big-eyed muppet-like creatures called  krumpuses  as someone who loves food but hates all  bugs i was delighted to find the bug  snacks all look adorable and charming  the key i think was giving them all arts  and crafts style googly eyes  pulling a page from pokemon each one has  a clever explanatory name  which they say aloud as they crawl  around exploring the various biomes of  snacktooth island  searching out all the inventive little  creatures scanning them to discover  their properties  and observing them in their element is a  pure delight there are 100 bug snacks  some of which are simply palette swap  reskins but finding a new one  is always exciting  to satisfy the former citizens of  snaxburg though you will need to do more  than look  getting your hands on delicious fridays  crapples and rebel peeds requires you to  be clever  catching each type of bug snack requires  a unique puzzle  each one has a different set of  characteristics that dictate how they  react to you  to your tools and to other bug snacks  some will run away when they see you  others will chase some can be caught  using your remote trap  while others will break free and need to  be incapacitated in some way before you  run in and scoop them up with a net  later on some of them are literally on  fire so you need to find a way to cool  them off before making your move  you have a tool kit that gives you a few  options for manipulating the snacks  your slingshot lets you fire different  sauces ketchup  hot sauce ranch chocolate and so on  which can act as bait or repellent  depending on what you're trying to catch  you have a tripwire that can knock over  aggressive creatures and bring down  snacks that are out of reach  more often though you'll need to use  your tools to bring two snacks together  and interact to make them susceptible to  capture  i wouldn't say any of them are tough to  catch but you need to think outside the  box  and that makes you feel clever when a  plan comes together  your interview subjects don't just want  you to catch their bug snacks  they want you to feed the snacks to them  too and when you feed them part of their  body will turn into the food they just  ate  or something related early on you gain  the ability to choose which body part  changes  which turns the bug snacks into cosmetic  items you can continue feeding bug  snacks to any character whenever you  want  giving them a makeover as increasingly  abstract food mutants  as a gameplay mechanic it's a bit  underwhelming in some later  optional missions certain colonists will  ask you to catch snacks with specific  colors or characteristics and apply them  to specific body parts  but that doesn't actually affect how you  catch the bug snacks or the feeding  process  the body changing factors into the story  so it never feels totally superfluous  but the actual mechanic is really just  for fooling around  bug snacks larger story plays out mainly  through the conversations you have with  the colonists once they've returned to  snaksburg  upon their return you get the chance to  interview each one learn more about  their personality and background  and get clues to the larger mysteries of  lizards disappearance and the origin of  the bug snacks  the overarching story is a proverbial  page turner motivating you to keep  moving through it  it's a bit predictable but that didn't  keep me from wanting to see how things  play out  the heart of bug snacks story isn't just  the plot but in its characters  though they look like cartoons colorful  and tropey  residents have real personalities and  personal stories to tell  if you want to hear them after  convincing them to return to town  each character has an optional quest  line in which you help them with their  work and or personal chores  befika the nosy former gossip columnist  asks you to spy on the other colonists  in the middle of the night  trifany the archaeologists wants help  exploring ancient ruins  invariably each character winds up  revealing that they're struggling with  deeper personal problems  difficulty coping with loss or failure  depression anxiety  sometimes you wind up helping them solve  those larger issues  but sometimes you don't even when you  can't though there are touching human  moments when these characters reveal  themselves to you  and shockingly having strawberry horns  or a burrito nose doesn't make them any  less relatable  nice work pal let's go home and we'll  count up the spoils  unsurprisingly bug snacks best qualities  are its cleverness and charm  the surprise and delight you feel when  you see a bug snack wiggling around or  watch someone eat one and change their  arm into food never goes away  that alone would make bug snacks worth  your time but creative puzzles and  thoughtful story give it the body and  depth to make a snack  feel more like a meal  [Music]
 

